WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.667
-Welcome back!
Guys, I am so excited,

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.133
because this weekend
is the Final Four.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.267
It is happening down
in New Orleans.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:07.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.467
These games are gonna be huge.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:12.167
You got Duke taking on
their rival North Carolina.

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:16.000
You have the Kansas Jayhawks
facing off against Villanova.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.467
It is impossible to predict
who's gonna go all the way.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:22.067
But you're in luck, because when
it comes to predicting things,

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.734
we have a secret weapon,
and it's...puppies.

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:26.834
It is time for
"The Puppy Predictors:

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:29.601
2022 Final Four Edition."

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:34.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
-♪ Puppy Predictors ♪

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:38.367
♪ Puppy Predictors ♪

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:39.767
-Welcome to
the "Puppy Predictors:

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:41.868
2022 Final Four Edition."

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.000
Here's how it works.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.434
We have eight puppies --
two for each team --

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:47.434
and one bowl of kibble.

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:51.033
Whichever team's puppy
gets to the bowl first

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:54.267
will determine who will be
crowned the national champs.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.801
Now, let's meet the puppies.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:01:01.300
For Duke, we have...
[ Audience "awws" ]

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:06.167
...Donna Braylon
and Kyle McAdams.

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:08.133
Good to see you, guys.

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:12.534
For North Carolina, we have...
[ Audience "awws" ]

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:17.234
...Mary Kennedy and Ted Mooney.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:21.167
For Kansas, we have...

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:22.534
[ Audience "awws" ]

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:26.434
...Roger Blain
and Lisa Armstrong.

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:29.334
And for Villanova, we have...

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.100
[ Audience "awws" ]
...Terry Jackson

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.033
and Gary Frick Jr.

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.601
Now...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.501
[ Chuckles ]
...before we release you

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:43.267
and we see who wins, I want to
keep this a clean, fair fight.

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:44.367
Hi, guys.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:46.834
A very fair fight.
Okay, no wandering.

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:48.534
No butt sniffing.

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:49.801
Let's keep this clean.

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.968
You guys,
whenever we're ready to go,

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:54.601
please release the puppies.

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.701
[ Audience "awws" ]

00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:02.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:04.467
[ Bell dinging ]
Oh! It's nail biter!

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:06.167
I think we have a winner.
Do we have...?

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:08.634
♪♪

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:10.467
Do we have instant replay?

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:12.234
Do we have instant replay?
Do we know who?

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:13.601
Was it North Carolina?

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:15.767
Let's play the scene in
slow motion and see who won.

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.033
♪♪

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:19.133
Ooh, it's such a close...

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:23.634
♪♪

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.133
It's like North -- Kansas,

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.634
but then North Carolina
sneaks in there.

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:30.734
Yeah, and gets in there.
It's North Carolina for the win!

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:36.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:39.033
Congratulations.
We have a winner right here.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.434
North Carolina
will be the champs,

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:43.701
the 2022 national champs.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.334
You heard it here first.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:47.067
Enjoy the Final Four, everybody.

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:48.868
We'll be right back
with Sienna Miller.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.501
Hey, you did well.
You did a great job.

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:52.734
Wanna go back down?

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:55.234
Wanna go eat?
Go eat. Go.

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:59.300
♪♪

